From: Spaceghost <spaceghost@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] lib: provide stpcpy for LLVM string folding

LLVM may fold a strcpy followed by a length calculation into stpcpy.  This
older kernel does not provide that freestanding string primitive, so supply
the conventional implementation alongside the other kernel string helpers.

---
 lib/string.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/string.c b/lib/string.c
index c9d7506..81ab972 100644
--- a/lib/string.c
+++ b/lib/string.c
@@ -1043,5 +1043,15 @@ int bcmp(const void *left, const void *right, size_t len)
 int bcmp(const void *left, const void *right, size_t len)
 {
 	return memcmp(left, right, len);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(bcmp);
+
+char *stpcpy(char *dest, const char *src)
+{
+	while ((*dest = *src) != '\0') {
+		dest++;
+		src++;
+	}
+	return dest;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(stpcpy);
-- 
